{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Each man by his banner, by the signs</b> — that Jacob hinted to them who would be head of a banner: whoever he spoke with face-to-face would be head of a banner, as in \"Reuben, you are my firstborn,\" \"Judah, you—your brothers shall praise you,\" \"Joseph—may El your father help you,\" \"Dan—I wait for Your salvation, YHWH.\"" "<b>opposite, surrounding the Tent</b> — in gematria: לאלפים אמה (to [a distance of] thousands of amah)." "<b>Surrounding the Tent of Meeting they shall encamp, and those encamping</b> — to teach: just as their encampment above is four banners surrounding the Throne of Glory, so below it was four banners surrounding the Tabernacle. This is \"awesome as bannered companies.\" This is \"His banner over me is love\" — for Israel saw at the time of the giving of the Torah the banners above and yearned for those banners. This is \"and in the name of our Elohim we will set up banners.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:03.870910618Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}